WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
Case 1: same pipeline, but this time the file is missing the country column. (Re-run I recorded after the fact.)

00:03.000 --> 00:09.000
Step 1: upload the case 1 file to S3 as input/orders.csv, replacing the normal one.

00:09.000 --> 00:14.000
Uploaded. Its header has every column except country.

00:14.000 --> 00:24.000
Step 2: run the pipeline in Rhombus, exactly as before. Nothing in the pipeline has changed.

00:24.000 --> 00:30.000
It stops at the cleaning step: "Pipeline failed at orders_cleaned". Good, it didn't push bad data out.

00:30.000 --> 00:35.000
The logs say why, but only as 'country'. No hint that a column is missing from the input.

00:35.000 --> 00:40.000
And right under the error, another line says "Pipeline execution completed successfully". Confusing.

00:40.000 --> 00:44.000
Step 3: check Google Cloud Storage.

00:44.000 --> 00:50.000
No new file. The newest one is still from my last good run. So it failed safely, it just explained it badly.
